      {
        "id": 188123,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-19T04:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint, although it was a largely un-fun slog. &nbsp; HP 7/7/7/6. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Despite trying to kill Ermine first, Ermine and Freight Train (Choke, plus the \"wipe out one person's hand unless everybody discards a card\") left me with few options from the get-go. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>It's weird -- I hadn't played many Vengeance games, so I played a large number of practice games (7+) before this one. &nbsp;In *every single game,* I managed to get Skycraper in Huge form by her 2nd round, and was able to lay waste effectively. &nbsp;In this game, she never had a single Huge card in hand until the very last turn, when she used Rest and Recover to pull it out of the trash. &nbsp;She was&nbsp;</span><span>stuck in Tiny form the whole game and couldn't come out, and never even had enough cards in her hand to use her Tiny power effectively; I think she played 3 links the entire game. &nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Likewise for Omni. &nbsp;His hand was also pretty devastated, and despite playing Reset and using his power on himself every turn to try to pull out extra cards, he never got the Ablative Coating he needed, or any of the \"play/draw extra cards\" Components. &nbsp;Two Disruptive Flechettes proved moderately useful.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Chrono plinked away every turn, but only ever had one bounty in play, and didn't get his Hat until mid-/late-game. &nbsp;Even then, like Sky-scraper, he never really had enough cards in his hand to do anything super-useful. &nbsp;He did manage to play his one bounty (\"By All Means\") on Ermine, and between that and Hunter and Hunted, it helped to take her down fast.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Tempest was the biggest damage dealer, via Grievous Hail Storm and the Gene-Bound Shackles.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Cyrus Hayes and the Sheriff were a big help in taking out the Nemeses, the Clones, and Friction's equipment.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Either way, not much fun on this challenge. &nbsp;No cool combos, no multi-card plays, no characters playing off each other...no real strategy at all. &nbsp;Just a battle of attrition: &nbsp;\"Heroes take their turn, do some damage,\" then \"villains take their turn, do some damage.\" &nbsp;The heroes had a few more HP to start, and did a little more damage every round, so they won, but not through any clever or inventive play on my part. &nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
