      {
        "id": 188126,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-19T15:40:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Blackfang108 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;TakeWalker wrote:<br><blockquote>That was a fun, easy Mint, and it taught me Omnitron has utility in Vengeance. :D (Granted, a few more games on my own showed he doesn't have&nbsp;<em>that</em> much, but he's definitely playable.)&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nI stuck an Ablative Coating and a Reactive Subroutine on him early, and he laid waste pretty effectively, honestly.&nbsp; But I think that's probably his best bet with these, unless he gets targeted by an Everyman's Strength Proletariat or a high-Surge Friction.\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;How'd you get out the Ablative Coating? &nbsp; In my game, Omni's hand got wiped out early by Ermine and the Fright Train card (the \"discard your entire hand unless everybody discards a card\" one-shot). &nbsp;I kept trying to get cards out for him, hoping for the Ablative Coating; I played every Reset I could get my hand on, and used his power to play extra cards from his hand every round, and never pulled an Ablative Coating. &nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I might be remembering another Vengence game I played with Omni around the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp; Not sure.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I let everyone discard a card.&nbsp;I've rarely used the \"drop your whole hand option\" unless one or two people have 1 card hands with cards I REALLY want to play.</p>",
