        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-19T18:30:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Blackfang108\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Blackfang108:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>robb8888 wrote:</b><br><blockquote><br>\n&nbsp;How'd you get out the Ablative Coating? &nbsp; In my game, Omni's hand got wiped out early by Ermine and the Fright Train card (the \"discard your entire hand unless everybody discards a card\" one-shot). &nbsp;I kept trying to get cards out for him, hoping for the Ablative Coating; I played every Reset I could get my hand on, and used his power to play extra cards from his hand every round, and never pulled an Ablative Coating. &nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI might be remembering another Vengence game I played with Omni around the same time.&nbsp;&nbsp; Not sure.&nbsp;I let everyone discard a card.&nbsp;I've rarely used the \"drop your whole hand option\" unless one or two people have 1 card hands with cards I REALLY want to play.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Same here – that was how Omni's hand got so low. &nbsp;Someone else got hit, but between Ermine pulling two Long Cons (everybody discard a card) and the Fright Train card (everybody discard a card), that was 3 cards down from everybody's hand. &nbsp;</p>",
