      {
        "id": 188132,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-25T20:25:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<div>OK, here it is.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Round 1:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Ermine: Chrono-Ranger discards Danny-Boy, Sky-Scraper discards Undetectable Relinking, Tempest discards Into the Stratosphere (because O-X is blowing up the Ongoings anyway), and O-X discards Reactive Plating Subroutine.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Chrono-Ranger plays Terrible Tech-Strike, dealing 2 to Ermine and 1+1 to Fright Train. &nbsp;Uses base power on Friction.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Proletariat does his thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Sky-Scraper plays Neutralizing Resonator on Fright Train, then uses her base power.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Fright Train does his thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Tempest plays Gene-Bound Shackles and uses his base power. &nbsp;Order / decisions matter a little; you can shoot yourself out of 1 damage to a Proletariat clone if you choose poorly. &nbsp;Basically, hit one clone (say \"no\"), hit the other clone, then hit Proletariat and say \"no\" again.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Friction does her thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Omnitron-X uses Sedative Flechettes and destroys Constant Prattle and Defensive Formation. &nbsp;Again, the damage order matters a little with Proletariat and clones. &nbsp;Hit the 5 HP clone, then Proletariat himself, then it doesn't matter anymore. &nbsp;Use base power on Tempest, put Grievous Hailstorm into play.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Silver Gulch plays Sustain the Portal. &nbsp;Do not discard, everything takes 2. &nbsp;Kill the Proletariat clones first.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Round 2:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Ermine does her thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Chrono Ranger plays Just Doin' My Job, which discards Ranger's Mark, Micro-Assembler, Shielding Winds, and Defensive Blast. &nbsp;CR pings Fright Train with JDMJ's damage, then uses base power on Fright Train.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Proletariat does his painful thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Sky-Scraper destroys Everyman's Strength with Neutralizing Resonator, plays Tectonic Chokeslam on the Shock Dampeners, and uses base power.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Fright Train does his thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Tempest plays Chain Lightning. Friction for 6, Fright Train for 6, Ermine for 4. &nbsp;Then, Grievous Hailstorm on Proletariat, Ermine, Friction, Crackjaw Crew, and Fright Train, in that order, to hit them all for 4.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Friction does her thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Omnitron-X plays reset and pulls Singularity. Plays Singularity, blows up Gene Bound Shackles. &nbsp;Use base power on Chrono-Ranger, Sudden Contract pulls By Any Means and puts it on Proletariat, pings Proletariat.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Silver Gulch plays Sustain the Portal again.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Round 3:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Ermine does her thing. &nbsp;I put Hailstorm back.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Chrono Ranger plays Eye on the Prize and pings Ermine, then draws The Whole Gang, playing it on Fright Train. &nbsp;Base power on FT, TWG destroys Proletariat.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Proletariat does his incap thing.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Sky-Scraper uses Tectonic Chokeslam and uses her base power to end the game.</div>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
